<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- NowCastTab — the body of the NowCast window: watch boxes + storm-based warnings, and today's storm
     reports. One of three mode bodies (see Controls/Windows/TemporalWindow, registered once per mode); the
     window supplies the surface, the title and the pin, so this is content only.
     ⚠️ The file keeps its "Tab" name from when the three were tabs of one Timeframe window. It is the same
     control, unchanged by the split; renaming all three would be churn. Bound to the coordinator MapViewModel.

       ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
       │ › [x] Radar                                          │  ← 24 px COMPACT headers (half the 48
       │ ⌄ [x] Warnings                                       │     SectionExpanderStyle gives)
       │  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────┐        │
       │  │ 7 active warnings                        │        │
       │  │ Updated 12:04 PM · checking every 15s    │        │
       │  └──────────────────────────────────────────┘        │
       │  [x] ■ Tornado                            0          │
       │  [x] ■ Severe thunderstorm                7          │
       │  Opacity ──────────────●  100%                       │  ← readout = the VM value
       │ › [-] Watches                                        │  [-] = some types ticked
       │ › [x] Storm reports                                  │
       └──────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘

     ⚠️ THE HEADER CHECKBOX IS A SELECT-ALL for its section (VM ToggleAll / AllShown): all ticked → clears
     them, otherwise ticks them all (a partial [-] goes to all on). IsChecked is ONE-WAY and the click calls
     the VM — the CheckBox's own toggle is overwritten by the VM's answer. Radar has no type rows, so its box
     is the layer show/hide (RadarViewModel.ShowRadarLayer). Clicking a box does not expand/collapse: the
     CheckBox handles the pointer before the header's ToggleButton sees it.
     ⚠️ EVERY BOX STARTS TICKED, and the map still launches clean: a tick means "draw while the mode runs"
     (IsModeActive, set in MapViewModel.OnTemporalModesChanged). Turning NowCast on brings them all up.

     ⚠️ COMPACT HEADERS ARE LOCAL to this window (NowCastCompactExpanderStyle + the Expander lightweight-
     styling overrides in Grid.Resources). Settings / PastCast / ForeCast keep the 48 px style. The chevron
     box is 32 px by default, which alone would hold the header at 34 — hence ExpanderChevronButtonSize.

     The body holds the "now"-oriented live-conditions options: the SPC Watch boxes and the storm-based
     Warning polygons (Tornado / Severe Thunderstorm). Both are active, event-driven current-conditions
     alerts, so they live under NowCast rather than ForeCast, in the UI and in the VM layer alike (their own
     WatchesViewModel / WarningsViewModel).

     EVERY SECTION IS AN EXPANDER (compact, based on Styles.xaml SectionExpanderStyle) — header = the
     select-all checkbox + the section title, body = its controls. Warnings is the only one open on load; the rest start closed, so the body starts
     short and you open what you came for. Expanded state is view-only and NOT persisted: reopening
     the window gives you these defaults again.
     ⚠️ The window opens at a FIXED full height (WindowManager's Left anchor), not sized to this body, so
     expanding enough sections can run the body past the window. That is known and accepted for now — a
     scroller is coming, hand-rolled rather than WinUI's.

     ⚠️ WARNINGS SITS ABOVE WATCHES, which puts it out of the map's Z-order (watches are drawn under
     warnings). Deliberate: it is the section you actually watch during severe weather, so it gets the
     slot under Radar rather than the one its layer order would give it.

     ⚠️ WATCHES AND WARNINGS ARE SEPARATE SECTIONS, not one "Watches and warnings". Each carries its
     OWN card describing its OWN active set, and one header cannot introduce two cards. They are also
     visually identical — the same two type rows, the same two colours — so the titles are the only
     thing telling you which is which.

     Both alert sections are the SAME control (Composites/PhenomOverlayInput) bound to a different view
     model, exactly as watches.js and warnings.js are the same JS factory with a different config. Storm
     reports stay their own control — the PastCast window shows that same block, so it is content of TWO
     hosts.

     ⚠️ This tab does NOT arm or clear NowCast; that is the NowCast key in the bottom bar's centre cluster.
     A tab body configures a mode, the key runs it. -->
<UserControl x:Class="Anvil.Controls.Composites.NowCastTab"
             xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
             xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
             xmlns:comp="using:Anvil.Controls.Composites"
             xmlns:d="http://schemas.microsoft.com/expression/blend/2008"
             xmlns:mc="http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006"
             mc:Ignorable="d">

    <Grid VerticalAlignment="Top" RowSpacing="8">
        <Grid.Resources>
            <!-- Expander lightweight styling (the template reads these by key), scoped to this window. -->
            <x:Double x:Key="ExpanderChevronButtonSize">20</x:Double>
            <Thickness x:Key="ExpanderChevronMargin">8,0,6,0</Thickness>
            <Thickness x:Key="ExpanderHeaderPadding">8,0,0,0</Thickness>

            <!-- The header is a UIElement here, so the base's string HeaderTemplate has to go. -->
            <Style x:Key="NowCastCompactExpanderStyle" TargetType="Expander"
                   BasedOn="{StaticResource SectionExpanderStyle}">
                <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="24"/>
                <Setter Property="HeaderTemplate" Value="{x:Null}"/>
            </Style>
            <!-- The 20 px glyph box and nothing else: no label, no min size, no padding. -->
            <Style x:Key="SectionHeaderCheckBoxStyle" TargetType="CheckBox">
                <Setter Property="MinWidth" Value="0"/>
                <Setter Property="MinHeight" Value="0"/>
                <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
            </Style>
            <Style x:Key="SectionHeaderTitleStyle" TargetType="TextBlock">
                <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="14"/>
                <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="SemiBold"/>
                <Setter Property="VerticalAlignment" Value="Center"/>
                <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{ThemeResource TextFillColorPrimaryBrush}"/>
            </Style>
        </Grid.Resources>
        <Grid.RowDefinitions>
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- radar -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- warnings -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- watches -->
            <RowDefinition Height="Auto"/> <!-- storm reports (today) -->
        </Grid.RowDefinitions>

        <!-- The radar layer everything else is drawn over; the value behind it is global, which is only
             safe because Past and Now are mutually exclusive so those two windows can't both be open.
             Its header box is the layer's show/hide - there are no type rows to select. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="0" Style="{StaticResource NowCastCompactExpanderStyle}">
            <Expander.Header>
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <CheckBox Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderCheckBoxStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar.ShowRadarLayer, Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnRadarHeaderClick"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Show radar layer"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show the radar layer"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="Radar" Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderTitleStyle}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Expander.Header>
            <comp:RadarOverlayInput ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Radar, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Expander>

        <!-- The imminent-threat polygons — open on load, and above Watches. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="1" IsExpanded="True" Style="{StaticResource NowCastCompactExpanderStyle}">
            <Expander.Header>
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <CheckBox Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderCheckBoxStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Warnings.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnWarningsHeaderClick"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Show all warnings"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show or hide every warning type"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="Warnings" Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderTitleStyle}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Expander.Header>
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput AlertNoun="warnings"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Warnings, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Expander>

        <!-- The large county-aggregated watch areas. Same control as Warnings above. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="2" Style="{StaticResource NowCastCompactExpanderStyle}">
            <Expander.Header>
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <CheckBox Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderCheckBoxStyle}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.Watches.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnWatchesHeaderClick"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Show all watches"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show or hide every watch type"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="Watches" Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderTitleStyle}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Expander.Header>
            <comp:PhenomOverlayInput AlertNoun="watches"
                                     ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.Watches, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Expander>

        <!-- ⚠️ The title is HERE, not inside StormReportsInput: that control is shared by BOTH temporal
             windows, and a window owns its own section structure while the control is just content.
             The header box carries the same IsReady gate as the type rows. -->
        <Expander Grid.Row="3" Style="{StaticResource NowCastCompactExpanderStyle}">
            <Expander.Header>
                <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="8">
                    <CheckBox Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderCheckBoxStyle}"
                              IsEnabled="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.IsReady, Mode=OneWay}"
                              IsChecked="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports.AllShown, Mode=OneWay}"
                              Click="OnStormReportsHeaderClick"
                              AutomationProperties.Name="Show all storm reports"
                              ToolTipService.ToolTip="Show or hide every report type"/>
                    <TextBlock Text="Storm reports" Style="{StaticResource SectionHeaderTitleStyle}"/>
                </StackPanel>
            </Expander.Header>
            <comp:StormReportsInput ViewModel="{x:Bind ViewModel.StormReports, Mode=OneWay}"/>
        </Expander>
    </Grid>
</UserControl>
